List all products that are more expensive than the average price of products within their own category.

SELECT p.product_name,p.category_id,p.price,p1.avg_price
FROM products p
WHERE price > ( SELECT avg(price) as avg_price
 FROM products p1
 WHERE p1.category_id=p.category_id
)

   OR
   
WITH cte_products AS (
  
  SELECT category_id,avg(price) as avg_price
  FROM products
  GROUP BY category_id
)
 SELECT p.product_name,p.category_id,p.price,p1.avg_price
 FROM products p
 JOIN cte_products p1 ON p.category_id=p1.category_id
 WHERE price > avg_price


  . It’s also more efficient than a correlated subquery because the average per category is computed once in the CTE, not repeatedly for each row.
